From bd336234e578d55243d9a9e4b9fd1cb7898fb33b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:42:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] ipa: simple: Focus and meter on the application's
 window

Tap to focus needs the focus window to follow the tap, and the
exposure to follow it too.

Support AfMetering and AfWindows: with AfMetering set to Windows, the
first window sets the focus window in the debayer parameters, in the
coordinates of the sensor's active area, which stand for the whole
picture (the simple pipeline has no ScalerCrop, and the statistics
cover what the output shows). A window is at least a tenth of the
picture a side. Continuous autofocus scans a new window; in auto mode
the application triggers the scan.

Support AeMeteringMode on the window's histogram: matrix (the whole
picture, as before and the default), spot (the window) and
centre-weighted (the whole picture with the window counted three
times).

Value-initialise the IPA context: configure() copies the previous
state before the first configuration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
